1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:04,127
Right triangle questions on the
SAT use a small set of tools:

2
00:00:04,147 --> 00:00:07,091
the Pythagorean theorem,
two special right triangles,

3
00:00:07,111 --> 00:00:08,734
and three trig ratios.

4
00:00:08,754 --> 00:00:11,805
You'll learn each one,
see how the SAT tests it,

5
00:00:11,825 --> 00:00:15,486
and work through seven practice
questions that get harder as they go.

6
00:00:15,506 --> 00:00:18,399
The most common mistake
isn't forgetting a formula.

7
00:00:18,433 --> 00:00:21,307
It's labeling the sides
from the wrong angle.

8
00:00:21,327 --> 00:00:24,683
Opposite and adjacent change
depending on where you're standing.

9
00:00:24,862 --> 00:00:28,255
Get that habit right, and most
of these questions get easier.

10
00:00:28,287 --> 00:00:31,910
Start with the Pythagorean theorem,
which is on the reference sheet.

11
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:34,910
a squared plus b squared equals c squared.

12
00:00:34,930 --> 00:00:37,695
The legs, a and b, form the right angle.

13
00:00:37,715 --> 00:00:40,838
The hypotenuse, c, is
across from the right angle,

14
00:00:40,858 --> 00:00:43,394
and it's always the longest side.

15
00:00:43,421 --> 00:00:46,151
The SAT loves whole-number
right triangles,

16
00:00:46,171 --> 00:00:48,171
called Pythagorean triples.

17
00:00:48,207 --> 00:00:49,472
Memorize three.

18
00:00:49,492 --> 00:00:52,151
Three, four, five.

19
00:00:52,171 --> 00:00:54,972
Five, twelve, thirteen.

20
00:00:54,992 --> 00:00:57,615
And eight, fifteen, seventeen.

21
00:00:57,635 --> 00:00:59,294
Their multiples work too.

22
00:00:59,314 --> 00:01:04,492
Six, eight, ten is just
three, four, five doubled.

23
00:01:04,562 --> 00:01:08,506
So if the legs are nine and twelve,
you don't need to square anything.

24
00:01:08,526 --> 00:01:11,648
Nine and twelve are three
and four, times three.

25
00:01:11,668 --> 00:01:14,862
So the hypotenuse is five times three,

26
00:01:14,882 --> 00:01:15,920
fifteen.

27
00:01:15,940 --> 00:01:18,277
Next, the two special right triangles,

28
00:01:18,297 --> 00:01:19,885
also on the reference sheet.

29
00:01:19,905 --> 00:01:23,169
In a forty-five,
forty-five, ninety triangle,

30
00:01:23,189 --> 00:01:27,812
the legs are equal, and the
hypotenuse is a leg times root two.

31
00:01:27,832 --> 00:01:32,187
So the sides are s, s, and s root two.

32
00:01:32,207 --> 00:01:36,222
In a thirty, sixty, ninety
triangle, the sides are x,

33
00:01:36,242 --> 00:01:38,600
x root three, and two x.

34
00:01:38,707 --> 00:01:42,563
The short side, x, is across
from the thirty degree angle.

35
00:01:42,635 --> 00:01:44,722
The hypotenuse is twice that.

36
00:01:44,742 --> 00:01:47,385
And x root three is across from the sixty.

37
00:01:47,435 --> 00:01:48,629
One warning.

38
00:01:48,649 --> 00:01:53,113
These ratios only work when the
angles really are forty-five,

39
00:01:53,149 --> 00:01:56,808
forty-five, ninety, or thirty, sixty,

40
00:01:56,828 --> 00:01:57,807
ninety.

41
00:01:57,827 --> 00:02:00,435
A triangle that just looks special isn't.

42
00:02:00,489 --> 00:02:01,826
Quick note on radians.

43
00:02:01,846 --> 00:02:04,683
If an angle is given
in radians, convert it.

44
00:02:04,703 --> 00:02:08,290
The reference sheet says a full
circle is three hundred sixty degrees,

45
00:02:08,310 --> 00:02:12,897
or two pi radians, so pi radians
is one hundred eighty degrees.

46
00:02:12,917 --> 00:02:17,183
Pi over six is thirty degrees,
pi over four is forty-five,

47
00:02:17,203 --> 00:02:19,647
and pi over three is sixty.

48
00:02:19,667 --> 00:02:21,595
Then use the same triangles.

49
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:23,354
Now trigonometry.

50
00:02:23,389 --> 00:02:25,834
For an acute angle in a right triangle,

51
00:02:25,854 --> 00:02:27,263
there are three ratios.

52
00:02:27,283 --> 00:02:29,977
Sine is opposite over hypotenuse.

53
00:02:29,997 --> 00:02:32,584
Cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse.

54
00:02:32,604 --> 00:02:35,140
Tangent is opposite over adjacent.

55
00:02:35,175 --> 00:02:37,533
The memory trick is soh cah toa.

56
00:02:37,610 --> 00:02:38,610
Here's the key.

57
00:02:38,717 --> 00:02:41,503
The hypotenuse never changes.

58
00:02:41,574 --> 00:02:44,662
But opposite and adjacent
depend on where you stand.

59
00:02:44,682 --> 00:02:47,768
From angle A, opposite is
the side across from A,

60
00:02:47,788 --> 00:02:50,859
and adjacent is the leg touching A.

61
00:02:50,896 --> 00:02:54,574
Move to angle B, and
those two legs swap jobs.

62
00:02:54,601 --> 00:02:58,172
That swap leads to a rule
the SAT tests directly.

63
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:01,903
The two acute angles in a right
triangle add up to ninety degrees,

64
00:03:01,923 --> 00:03:04,958
and the side opposite A is adjacent to B.

65
00:03:05,030 --> 00:03:08,127
So sine of A equals cosine of B.

66
00:03:08,147 --> 00:03:14,198
In general, sine of x degrees equals
cosine of ninety minus x degrees.

67
00:03:14,218 --> 00:03:18,162
Sine of twenty degrees equals
cosine of seventy degrees.

68
00:03:18,182 --> 00:03:22,090
So when sine of one acute
angle equals cosine of another,

69
00:03:22,110 --> 00:03:24,393
the two angles add up to ninety.

70
00:03:24,413 --> 00:03:25,413
Last idea.

71
00:03:25,699 --> 00:03:28,536
Trig ratios depend only on the angles,

72
00:03:28,556 --> 00:03:30,735
not on the size of the triangle.

73
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:33,965
So similar right triangles
share the same sine,

74
00:03:33,985 --> 00:03:35,519
cosine, and tangent.

75
00:03:35,698 --> 00:03:39,465
Scale a three, four,
five triangle up to six,

76
00:03:39,485 --> 00:03:43,875
eight, ten, and the sine of the
matching angle is still three fifths.

77
00:03:43,895 --> 00:03:45,467
Here's how to spot what you need.

78
00:03:45,610 --> 00:03:47,860
Two sides, and they want the third?

79
00:03:48,038 --> 00:03:51,110
Pythagorean theorem,
and look for a triple.

80
00:03:51,252 --> 00:03:54,180
Thirty, forty-five, or sixty degrees?

81
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:56,003
Special triangles.

82
00:03:56,073 --> 00:03:59,003
Asked for a sine, cosine, or tangent?

83
00:03:59,253 --> 00:04:01,360
Draw it, and label from that angle.

84
00:04:01,409 --> 00:04:04,622
Sine of one expression
equals cosine of another?

85
00:04:04,695 --> 00:04:05,960
Add them to ninety.

86
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:07,409
Similar triangles?

87
00:04:07,445 --> 00:04:09,266
Copy the ratio across.

88
00:04:09,373 --> 00:04:13,746
And a non-special angle usually
means an answer written with sine,

89
00:04:13,766 --> 00:04:15,373
cosine, or tangent.

90
00:04:15,457 --> 00:04:16,401
Question one.

91
00:04:16,421 --> 00:04:19,258
A twenty foot ladder leans
against a vertical wall.

92
00:04:19,278 --> 00:04:21,401
The bottom of the ladder
is on level ground,

93
00:04:21,421 --> 00:04:23,366
twelve feet from the base of the wall.

94
00:04:23,386 --> 00:04:27,524
How many feet above the ground does
the top of the ladder touch the wall?

95
00:04:27,544 --> 00:04:28,830
Pause and try it.

96
00:04:32,086 --> 00:04:33,959
The wall and the ground
make the right angle,

97
00:04:33,979 --> 00:04:37,030
so the ladder, across from
it, is the hypotenuse:

98
00:04:37,050 --> 00:04:37,995
twenty.

99
00:04:38,015 --> 00:04:39,244
Twelve is a leg.

100
00:04:39,264 --> 00:04:41,173
Twelve and twenty are three and five,

101
00:04:41,193 --> 00:04:42,172
times four.

102
00:04:42,192 --> 00:04:46,852
So it's a three, four, five
triangle scaled by four,

103
00:04:46,872 --> 00:04:49,209
and the missing leg is four times four,

104
00:04:49,229 --> 00:04:49,959
sixteen.

105
00:04:49,979 --> 00:04:51,943
The answer is B.

106
00:04:51,981 --> 00:04:57,282
Check: twelve squared plus sixteen squared
is one forty-four plus two fifty-six,

107
00:04:57,302 --> 00:05:00,159
which is four hundred, twenty squared.

108
00:05:00,195 --> 00:05:01,603
The trap is C.

109
00:05:01,623 --> 00:05:04,960
It treats the ladder as a
leg and adds the squares.

110
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:08,266
A and D just subtract and add the sides.

111
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:09,487
Question two.

112
00:05:10,057 --> 00:05:14,594
In right triangle J K L,
angle K is a right angle,

113
00:05:14,808 --> 00:05:18,593
J K equals twenty, and
K L equals twenty-one.

114
00:05:19,021 --> 00:05:21,648
What is the value of sine of L?

115
00:05:21,668 --> 00:05:22,954
Pause and try it.

116
00:05:26,210 --> 00:05:28,404
There's no figure, so draw one.

117
00:05:28,424 --> 00:05:30,031
Put the right angle at K.

118
00:05:30,138 --> 00:05:32,868
The hypotenuse is across
from K, so it's J L.

119
00:05:32,888 --> 00:05:35,654
Twenty and twenty-one
aren't a triple you know,

120
00:05:35,674 --> 00:05:37,067
so use the theorem.

121
00:05:37,137 --> 00:05:40,332
Four hundred plus four
forty-one is eight forty-one,

122
00:05:40,352 --> 00:05:42,388
and its square root is twenty-nine.

123
00:05:42,494 --> 00:05:43,724
Now stand at L.

124
00:05:43,744 --> 00:05:47,331
The side opposite L is
J K, which is twenty.

125
00:05:47,351 --> 00:05:49,458
The hypotenuse is twenty-nine.

126
00:05:49,530 --> 00:05:52,331
So sine of L is twenty over twenty-nine.

127
00:05:52,351 --> 00:05:54,493
The answer is C.

128
00:05:54,521 --> 00:05:57,573
Every other choice is a real
ratio from this triangle,

129
00:05:57,593 --> 00:06:00,858
just the wrong one:
cosine of L, tangent of L,

130
00:06:00,878 --> 00:06:04,335
and tangent of J, which is
labeled from the wrong angle.

131
00:06:04,355 --> 00:06:05,478
Question three.

132
00:06:05,498 --> 00:06:08,799
In right triangle P Q R,
angle Q is a right angle,

133
00:06:08,819 --> 00:06:13,641
angle P measures sixty degrees,
and P R equals fourteen.

134
00:06:13,711 --> 00:06:15,569
What is the length of Q R?

135
00:06:15,589 --> 00:06:16,874
Pause and try it.

136
00:06:20,131 --> 00:06:23,289
Angle Q is ninety and angle P is sixty,

137
00:06:23,309 --> 00:06:25,218
so angle R is thirty.

138
00:06:25,238 --> 00:06:28,075
It's a thirty, sixty, ninety triangle.

139
00:06:28,095 --> 00:06:31,361
P R is across from the right
angle, so it's the hypotenuse,

140
00:06:31,381 --> 00:06:32,253
two x.

141
00:06:32,273 --> 00:06:35,166
Two x equals fourteen, so x is seven.

142
00:06:35,203 --> 00:06:39,203
Q R is across from angle
P, the sixty degree angle.

143
00:06:39,275 --> 00:06:42,540
The side across from
sixty is x root three.

144
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:44,898
So Q R is seven root three.

145
00:06:44,918 --> 00:06:46,489
The answer is D.

146
00:06:46,542 --> 00:06:49,449
Seven is P Q, the side
across from the thirty.

147
00:06:49,469 --> 00:06:52,557
Seven root two uses the
forty-five, forty-five,

148
00:06:52,577 --> 00:06:53,771
ninety ratio.

149
00:06:53,791 --> 00:06:57,307
And fourteen root three treats the
hypotenuse like the short side.

150
00:06:57,327 --> 00:07:00,938
Always match each side to
the angle across from it.

151
00:07:00,958 --> 00:07:05,831
Before the harder questions, here are the
three traps behind most wrong answers.

152
00:07:05,851 --> 00:07:08,673
One: mixing up opposite and adjacent,

153
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:11,315
usually by labeling from the wrong angle.

154
00:07:11,387 --> 00:07:14,296
Two: using the hypotenuse as a leg.

155
00:07:14,316 --> 00:07:18,816
Three: using special triangle ratios
on a triangle that isn't special.

156
00:07:18,873 --> 00:07:21,925
Here's a question built
on traps one and three.

157
00:07:21,945 --> 00:07:25,909
In right triangle A B C,
angle C is a right angle,

158
00:07:26,122 --> 00:07:28,460
angle A measures thirty-five degrees,

159
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:30,265
and A B equals ten.

160
00:07:30,373 --> 00:07:33,313
Which expression represents
the length of B C?

161
00:07:33,333 --> 00:07:34,619
Pause and try it.

162
00:07:37,875 --> 00:07:38,712
Stand at A.

163
00:07:38,732 --> 00:07:41,445
B C is across from A, so it's opposite.

164
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:43,497
A B is the hypotenuse.

165
00:07:43,517 --> 00:07:45,819
Opposite over hypotenuse is sine.

166
00:07:45,839 --> 00:07:49,731
So sine of thirty-five
degrees equals B C over ten,

167
00:07:49,803 --> 00:07:53,676
and B C equals ten times
sine of thirty-five degrees.

168
00:07:53,696 --> 00:07:55,362
The answer is A.

169
00:07:55,382 --> 00:07:58,095
B is the adjacent side, A C.

170
00:07:58,167 --> 00:08:01,862
C uses tangent, but tangent
never involves the hypotenuse.

171
00:08:01,882 --> 00:08:04,754
And D, five, is half the hypotenuse.

172
00:08:04,774 --> 00:08:08,326
That only works for the side
across from a thirty degree angle.

173
00:08:08,346 --> 00:08:10,013
Thirty-five isn't special.

174
00:08:10,033 --> 00:08:13,370
And notice: angle B is fifty-five degrees.

175
00:08:13,390 --> 00:08:19,248
So the same length could be written as
ten times cosine of fifty-five degrees.

176
00:08:19,283 --> 00:08:22,425
That's the complement rule,
and it's the next question.

177
00:08:22,445 --> 00:08:23,353
Question five.

178
00:08:23,373 --> 00:08:29,425
In the equation, sine of the quantity
two k plus thirteen degrees equals cosine

179
00:08:29,445 --> 00:08:32,388
of the quantity three
k minus eight degrees,

180
00:08:32,408 --> 00:08:37,210
k is a constant, and both angle measures
are between zero and ninety degrees.

181
00:08:37,230 --> 00:08:39,015
What is the value of k?

182
00:08:39,035 --> 00:08:40,320
Pause and try it.

183
00:08:44,576 --> 00:08:47,806
Sine of one acute angle
equals cosine of another,

184
00:08:47,826 --> 00:08:49,806
so the angles add to ninety.

185
00:08:49,826 --> 00:08:53,091
Two k plus thirteen,
plus three k minus eight,

186
00:08:53,111 --> 00:08:54,342
equals ninety.

187
00:08:54,362 --> 00:08:57,270
That's five k plus five equals ninety.

188
00:08:57,290 --> 00:09:01,120
So five k is eighty-five,
and k is seventeen.

189
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:04,335
Check: the angles are forty-seven
and forty-three degrees,

190
00:09:04,355 --> 00:09:06,799
both acute, and they add to ninety.

191
00:09:06,819 --> 00:09:09,085
The trap is setting the angles equal.

192
00:09:09,105 --> 00:09:12,835
That gives k equals twenty-one
and two fifty-five degree angles,

193
00:09:12,855 --> 00:09:14,980
which add to one hundred ten.

194
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,250
Question six.

195
00:09:16,464 --> 00:09:20,552
In right triangle R S T,
angle T is a right angle,

196
00:09:20,572 --> 00:09:22,587
and cosine of R equals eight seventeenths.

197
00:09:22,607 --> 00:09:29,837
Triangle U V W is similar
to triangle R S T,

198
00:09:29,857 --> 00:09:34,194
with U, V, and W corresponding to R, S,

199
00:09:34,214 --> 00:09:35,105
and T.

200
00:09:35,125 --> 00:09:39,911
If U V equals fifty-one,
what is the length of V W?

201
00:09:39,942 --> 00:09:41,227
Pause and try it.

202
00:09:45,483 --> 00:09:48,249
Similar triangles share their trig ratios.

203
00:09:48,269 --> 00:09:53,142
U matches R, so cosine of U
is also eight seventeenths.

204
00:09:53,162 --> 00:09:56,677
And W matches T, so W is the right angle.

205
00:09:56,697 --> 00:10:00,698
That makes U V, across
from W, the hypotenuse.

206
00:10:00,753 --> 00:10:04,483
Cosine is adjacent over
hypotenuse, so this is an eight,

207
00:10:04,503 --> 00:10:09,626
fifteen, seventeen triangle, and the
side across from U is the fifteen part.

208
00:10:09,646 --> 00:10:14,983
Fifty-one is seventeen times three,
so every side is three times bigger.

209
00:10:15,003 --> 00:10:18,575
V W is fifteen times three, forty-five.

210
00:10:18,677 --> 00:10:21,336
If you got twenty-four, you
found the adjacent side,

211
00:10:21,356 --> 00:10:21,443
U W.

212
00:10:21,463 --> 00:10:26,071
The question asks for V
W, the side across from U.

213
00:10:26,091 --> 00:10:27,948
Last one, and the hardest.

214
00:10:28,305 --> 00:10:32,571
In triangle A B C, point
D lies on side B C,

215
00:10:32,591 --> 00:10:36,233
and segment A D is
perpendicular to side B C.

216
00:10:36,305 --> 00:10:40,857
Angle B measures forty-five degrees,
angle C measures thirty degrees,

217
00:10:40,877 --> 00:10:42,912
and A D equals six.

218
00:10:43,127 --> 00:10:45,198
What is the length of B C?

219
00:10:45,218 --> 00:10:45,912
Pause and try it.

220
00:10:45,932 --> 00:10:47,718
Take a little longer on this one.

221
00:10:51,914 --> 00:10:55,966
The altitude splits the big
triangle into two right triangles.

222
00:10:55,986 --> 00:11:00,394
On the left, triangle A B D has
a forty-five degree angle at B,

223
00:11:00,414 --> 00:11:03,823
so it's forty-five, forty-five, ninety.

224
00:11:03,843 --> 00:11:06,609
The legs are equal, so B D equals A D,

225
00:11:06,629 --> 00:11:07,771
which is six.

226
00:11:07,823 --> 00:11:11,339
On the right, triangle A D C
has a thirty degree angle at C,

227
00:11:11,359 --> 00:11:14,073
so it's thirty, sixty, ninety.

228
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:17,053
A D is across from the thirty,
so it's the short side:

229
00:11:17,073 --> 00:11:18,430
x equals six.

230
00:11:18,608 --> 00:11:21,303
D C is across from the
sixty degree angle at A,

231
00:11:21,323 --> 00:11:23,103
so it's six root three.

232
00:11:23,123 --> 00:11:26,174
B C is the two pieces together:
six plus six root three.

233
00:11:26,194 --> 00:11:27,682
The answer is B.

234
00:11:27,702 --> 00:11:29,932
A assumes both halves are forty-five,

235
00:11:29,952 --> 00:11:31,844
forty-five, ninety.

236
00:11:32,202 --> 00:11:34,432
C divides by root three
instead of multiplying,

237
00:11:34,452 --> 00:11:38,966
which makes the side across from sixty
shorter than the side across from thirty.

238
00:11:38,986 --> 00:11:42,559
And D adds the two slanted
sides instead of the base.

239
00:11:42,610 --> 00:11:45,538
Here's the method for any
right triangle question.

240
00:11:45,644 --> 00:11:48,947
Step one: draw it, even
if there's a figure,

241
00:11:48,967 --> 00:11:50,645
and mark the right angle.

242
00:11:50,752 --> 00:11:54,054
Step two: put your finger
on the angle they ask about,

243
00:11:54,074 --> 00:11:57,788
and label hypotenuse, opposite,
and adjacent from there.

244
00:11:57,830 --> 00:12:01,115
Step three: look for a
shortcut before you calculate.

245
00:12:01,222 --> 00:12:04,739
A triple, a special angle,
a sine equal to a cosine,

246
00:12:04,759 --> 00:12:06,223
or a similar triangle.

247
00:12:06,330 --> 00:12:10,595
Step four: write the ratio, solve,
